---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";

const credibilityStats = [
  { value: "25,000+", label: "Doors Knocked" },
  { value: "10,000+", label: "Sales Conversations" },
  { value: "50-60%", label: "Current Close Rate" },
  { value: "500+", label: "Websites & Landing Pages Built" },
  { value: "100K+", label: "Social Media Followers" },
  { value: "100s", label: "Businesses Taught (Courses & YouTube)" },
];

const founders = [
  {
    name: "Tye Norden",
    role: "Co-Founder",
    image: "https://storage.googleapis.com/msgsndr/6B4reCngPYfDkJwOtiM0/media/ac4470f1-66de-4a33-b18e-2842f005e148.jpeg",
    paragraphs: [
      "Tye is the co-founder of The Lead Venture, where he leads sales. He holds a bachelor's degree in marketing from Bowling Green State University and spent 3 years in residential home exterior sales — roofing specifically — generating $1.3 million gross and $800K+ net, including more than $1 million in residential sales in under a single year. He worked both sides of the business, production and sales, and out-produced almost everyone around him, Jonathan included: more leads generated, more doors knocked, and a knack for turning a cold conversation into a sale.",
      "Outside of home exteriors, Tye is a super affiliate. He's built an audience of 100,000+ followers and regularly pulls in millions of views a month, with a peak month north of 100 million views. One promotion alone generated 6,000–7,000 buyers off his list, with roughly 1,000 recurring weekly buyers at its peak. He also owns and operates a physical poker club and holds real estate investments, on top of running a multi six-figure-a-year super affiliate business.",
      "That mix — direct sales, affiliate marketing, content creation, and real estate — gives him a wide-angle view of what actually drives growth for a business, not just theory. At The Lead Venture, Tye brings that same results-first approach to helping local service businesses sell more, close faster, and grow with confidence.",
    ],
  },
  {
    name: "Jonathan Blake",
    role: "Co-Founder",
    image: "https://storage.googleapis.com/msgsndr/6B4reCngPYfDkJwOtiM0/media/babb3410-7d25-4408-8cd3-f11a437f4b38.jpg",
    paragraphs: [
      "I grew up severely dyslexic and barely scraped through school. The traditional path wasn't built for me, so I built my own. I discovered online marketing and self-education, and it changed everything.",
      "In college, before any of that, I ran a pay-per-performance agency for home remodeling companies — I managed their Google Ads, built their funnels, set up their automation, then personally called and qualified every lead, booked the estimate, and followed up afterward. It was commission-only, so I learned a hard lesson early: most of those businesses weren't failing because of bad leads. They were failing because owners wouldn't answer the phone, never updated their CRM, and didn't know how to sell to a cold audience. That's the exact gap The Lead Venture is built to close.",
      "I also dropped out of college to help a friend run a turnaround agency for medical spas across the Northeast. We ran their Facebook ads to get people in the door, then taught the staff how to consultatively sell $2,500–$8,500+ high-ticket memberships, with a structured downsell for anyone who said no. We lined the office with before-and-afters and sold straight off a resell intake form, customized to the client. It worked because the system did the selling, not raw pressure.",
      "In 2015, I started a tree service. I didn't just learn how to cut trees, I had to learn how to survive. I struggled for years figuring out how to market, sell, create irresistible offers, and build websites that actually converted. Once I cracked the code, I ran that business for 5 years and scaled it to six figures a month before moving on in 2020. Before that, I'd also done the marketing and sales for my dad's home remodeling business.",
      "Starting in 2018, I took on marketing and sales clients across more industries than most agencies touch in a decade: tree services, golf courses, home remodeling, dog waste removal, pest control, roofing and gutters, junk removal (websites and video), churches (websites and logos), about a dozen lawn care companies, and barbershops (content creation and SMS marketing).",
      "Then I pivoted into residential home exterior sales, door to door. I knocked on 25,000 doors, had over 10,000 conversations, and personally closed more than 1,000 leads. In non-insurance exterior sales alone — no storm claims, straight retail — I generated over $1 million, netting $800K in a single year.",
      "Today, I run a lawn care and landscaping business with a $1.3 million book of maintenance contracts and about $2 million in total revenue once enhancement work is added in, on top of personally selling millions of dollars in lawn care services over the years. I also sell for a lawn and hardscape company doing commercial and residential work, closing 50-60% of my leads the past several months: speed to lead under 60 seconds, same-day or next-day appointments only, both decision-makers at the table, a full presentation, then a direct ask for the sale — one-call close. If they say no, I follow up, friend them on Facebook and Instagram, like and comment on their posts, and ask for a referral anyway. It's the same follow-up-first system we put in Booked Solid, and it's why our clients get more than just a website. I've been doing marketing and sales since 2015, I've run Facebook ad campaigns for my own businesses and for more than 30 others, and I've taught hundreds of business owners through courses and YouTube.",
    ],
  },
];

const journey = [
  { year: "College", title: "Learning to Sell", desc: "Running a pay-per-performance agency for remodelers and a high-ticket turnaround agency for med spas — the first lessons in building systems that sell without hype." },
  { year: "2015", title: "In the Trenches", desc: "Building a tree service from scratch, scaling it to six figures a month over 5 years. Learning the hard lessons of local marketing, sales, and survival." },
  { year: "2018", title: "Full-Service Agency", desc: "Taking on marketing and sales clients across a dozen-plus industries — golf courses, churches, junk removal, pest control, roofing, barbershops, and more." },
  { year: "2020", title: "The Pivot", desc: "Moving into residential home exterior sales, door to door. Knocking 25,000 doors, 10,000+ conversations, and generating over $1M in non-insurance exterior sales — $800K net in year one." },
  { year: "2022", title: "Mastering Sales", desc: "Selling millions in direct sales. Combining field production experience with high-ticket closing strategies." },
  { year: "Today", title: "The Lead Venture", desc: "Running a $1.3M+ lawn care book of business, building 500+ websites and landing pages, and writing Booked Solid — the playbook behind it all." },
];

const bookedSolidPromises = [
  "Price jobs for real profit",
  "Close more jobs on the first visit",
  "Build a team that runs without you",
  "Turn customers into a referral engine",
];
---

<Layout title="Meet the Team" description="We Know The Grind Because We've Lived It — meet the founders of The Lead Venture.">
  <section class="bg-[#1A1D27] py-24 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-(--breakpoint-xl) px-5">
      <div class="mb-16 text-center">
        <h1 class="font-heading text-4xl font-black uppercase leading-tight tracking-tight md:text-6xl">
          We Know The Grind Because <span class="text-accent-400">We've Lived It.</span>
        </h1>
      </div>

      <div class="mx-auto mb-20 grid max-w-5xl grid-cols-2 gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
        {credibilityStats.map((stat) => (
          <div class="text-center">
            <div class="font-heading text-3xl font-black text-accent-400 md:text-4xl">{stat.value}</div>
            <div class="mt-2 text-sm text-white/60">{stat.label}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl space-y-20">
        {founders.map((founder, i) => (
          <div class={`grid items-start gap-12 md:grid-cols-2 ${i % 2 === 1 ? "md:[&>*:first-child]:order-2" : ""}`}>
            <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/80">
              <h2 class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3 text-3xl font-bold text-white">
                {founder.name}
                <span class="rounded-full bg-accent-500/10 px-3 py-1 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent-400">{founder.role}</span>
              </h2>
              {founder.paragraphs.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
            </div>
            <div class="relative min-h-[400px] md:sticky md:top-24">
              <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-10 scale-90 rounded-full bg-accent-500/20 blur-[60px]"></div>
              <img
                src={founder.image}
                alt={`${founder.name} — Co-Founder`}
                loading="lazy"
                class="h-full w-full rounded-3xl border border-white/10 object-cover shadow-2xl"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="mx-auto mt-32 max-w-4xl">
        <h3 class="mb-16 text-center text-3xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight">The Journey</h3>
        <div class="relative ml-4 space-y-12 border-l-2 border-accent-500/30 md:ml-[50%]">
          {journey.map((item, i) => (
            <div class="relative pl-8 md:pl-0">
              <div class={i % 2 === 0 ? "md:-ml-[100%] md:w-[calc(100%-2rem)] md:pr-12 md:text-right" : "md:w-[calc(100%-2rem)] md:pl-12"}>
                <div class="absolute left-[-9px] top-1 h-4 w-4 rounded-full bg-accent-500 shadow-[0_0_15px_rgba(255,138,30,0.6)]"></div>
                <div class="mb-1 text-xl font-bold text-accent-400">{item.year}</div>
                <h4 class="mb-2 text-xl font-bold text-white">{item.title}</h4>
                <p class="text-white/70">{item.desc}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mx-auto mt-32 max-w-4xl rounded-lg border border-accent-500/50 bg-white/5 p-8 md:p-12">
        <p class="mb-2 text-center text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent-400">We Literally Wrote The Book On This</p>
        <h3 class="mb-6 text-center font-heading text-3xl font-black uppercase tracking-tight md:text-4xl">Booked Solid</h3>
        <p class="mx-auto mb-6 max-w-2xl text-center text-lg text-white/70">
          The Local Service Business Playbook for Endless Leads, Bigger Margins, and a Reputation That Lasts — the exact system we've run for the last decade, put down on paper by both co-founders.
        </p>
        <p class="mx-auto mb-10 max-w-xl text-center font-heading text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide text-accent-400">
          Get Booked. Get Paid. Get Back To Living.
        </p>
        <div class="mx-auto mb-10 grid max-w-2xl gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          {bookedSolidPromises.map((promise) => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl bg-white/5 p-4">
              <span class="mt-0.5 text-accent-400">✓</span>
              <span class="text-white/80">{promise}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center text-white/60">
          18 chapters across 12 parts, a full case study, a 90-day action calendar, a resource appendix, a glossary, and a one-page system map — everything in it is the same playbook behind the strategy we build into every website we launch.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 text-center">
          <a href="/contact" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-accent-500 px-8 py-3 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent-400 transition hover:bg-accent-500 hover:text-white">
            Ask About Getting a Copy →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="relative mx-auto mt-20 max-w-3xl rounded-lg border border-accent-500/50 bg-white/5 p-8 text-center md:p-12">
        <h3 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold uppercase">P.S. If you're a skimmer, here's the bottom line:</h3>
        <p class="mb-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/80">
          We are fully building out your complete, rugged, local SEO website engine completely free of charge. Your custom preview link will hit your inbox in as little as 72 hours. There is no catch, no long-term contracts, and no obligation. If you love the site and want to push it live to start dominating your local market, you just cover the secure cloud hosting framework or let us deploy it seamlessly for you.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact" class="inline-flex w-full items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-accent-500 px-10 py-4 text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-white transition hover:bg-accent-600 sm:w-auto">
          Claim Your Free Build →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
